			"Message": "feat(Mist): Add comprehensive architectural documentation for DNS isolation server\n\nIntroduce the `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` file for the Mist component, detailing its role as a local DNS server providing network isolation for Land's sidecar processes.\n\nThe document outlines the authoritative `editor.land` zone configuration, forward allowlisting mechanisms for external domain access, and DNSSEC signing using ECDSA P-256. It includes mermaid diagrams illustrating the interaction between `Server.rs`, `Zone.rs`, `Resolver.rs`, and `ForwardSecurity.rs`, alongside the `WebSocket.rs` transport layer for Sky-to-Cocoon communication.\n\nThis documentation clarifies the startup sequence, module responsibilities, and security boundaries enforced by Mist to prevent data exfiltration through DNS.",
			"SHA": "f3982893222ec6f20c538f3ed5b8912cc7c76133"
		},
